Hello, It's been a while since I posted my last writing. I've learned lot of things in the past years.
My goal is still unchanged, it is to create a new and faster and simpler compiler backend for haskell and possible for other functional languages.
But there is a change in the design and implementation, I switched to Idris2.
This means that the first part of my haskell compiler pipeline will use GHC for haskell frontend, but the second part will be written in idris2.
The first part of the pipeline (GHC) will parse, typecheck and optimize core and save the result to external stg files.
Then the estg ir will be read by the backend that will be written in idris2, more specifically staged idris2. Let me elaborate this design.
